-- title:
--   Polar differentials under constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq K'$ and $F \subseteq F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra and compatible algebra maps $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$, $K \to F'$ making the relevant scalar towers and commutation of $K'$- and $F$-actions on $F'$ hold, with $K$ and $K'$ algebraically closed. Assume $F/K$ and $F'/K'$ each satisfy `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero element has a degree-zero divisor recording its orders at all places, every place has residue field finite over the constant field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the function field; assume also that $F$ is essentially of finite type over $K$ and $F'$ over $K'$. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ that contains the image of $K$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring. Further hypotheses: there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite over $K(x)$, and likewise $x' \in F'$ over $K'$ (`hfg`, `hfg'`); the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$ (`hgen`); and at every place $v$ of $F/K$, respectively $w$ of $F'/K'$, the differential $d\pi_v$ of the chosen uniformizer spans the differentials over the function field (`hdK`, `hdK'`). Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/K$, and let $S'$ be the set of places $w$ of $F'/K'$ whose valuation subring pulls back along $F \to F'$ to the valuation subring of some $v \in S$. Write $\Omega(S)$ for the $K$-submodule of $\Omega[F/K]$ of those $\omega$ such that at each $v \notin S$ one has $\omega = f \cdot d\pi_v$ with $f$ in the valuation subring of $v$, and at each $v \in S$ one has $\omega = f \cdot d\pi_v$ with $\pi_v f$ in that valuation subring; define $\Omega(S') \subseteq \Omega[F'/K']$ analogously. The conclusion is the conjunction: the base-change map $\Omega[F/K] \to \Omega[F'/K']$ carries $\Omega(S)$ into $\Omega(S')$, and every element of $\Omega(S')$ lies in the $K'$-span of the image of $\Omega(S)$.
--
--   This is the compatibility of differentials with prescribed simple poles with a constant field extension of algebraically closed constant fields: the image of the $K$-space of differentials regular off $S$ with at most simple poles on $S$ spans, over $K'$, the corresponding space upstairs. It is used in the construction of an injective map out of $K' \otimes_K \Omega(S)$ for the supersingular polar differentials on a modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_map_mem_polarDifferentials_and_mem_span_image_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed.lean

